warmed, days and nights alike","rain":"Marquette has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 33\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>33\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 39\u00b0F, and the record is 66\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>28\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Marquette's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Marquette has set <strong>79 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 146 that chance alone would give, and <strong>169 record highs</strong>, close to the 146 that chance alone would give. The 2000s hold the most record highs of any decade (72). Marquette's all-time high is 99\u00b0F, on June 30, 1963.","t_chg":"Marquette has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 66 complete years: Marquette's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.62\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.41 to +0.83), about +4.0\u00b0F since 1960. Marquette's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.34\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.14 to +0.54), about +2.2\u00b0F since 1960.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 7 of 12 months. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Marquette has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Marquette's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+1.21 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.37 to +2.06), about +7.8 inches since 1961. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 36.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 1985 (51.59 in); the driest, 1961 (22.24 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}